br0w+@andrew.cmu.edu (Bruno W. Repetto) writes:

{B} Some minor quirks I found:
{B}  - Vlad the Impaler should be improved. By the time I get to him, he
       is a wimp by comparison.

Ditto.

{B} Questions:
{B}  - Has the BIG LEVEL been implemented as an option?

Yes.  If you are using the "official" pl9 binary, all options are implemented.

BTW, the big level is not a compile time option.  It's always there.

{B}    I've never encountered it in my PC NH 3.09, from which I suspect
{B}    that such an option was turned off during compilation for PCs.
{B}    Is this true?

To be sure, get into wizard mode, press ^O, then teleport to the "Big:" level.
There is only a 1 in 15 chance that there is a big level in a normal game, but
there is always a big level in wizard mode.

{B}  - Is there a way to gain an intrinsic that protects one of being
       paralyzed by gelatinous cubes and the like once one is powerful enough?

No.

{B}  - Should blessed scrolls of genocide wipe out entire classes of monsters?
{B}    (I.e., if one responds with a 'T', trolls, ice trolls, rock trolls, water
{B}    trolls, olog hais would be history)

Yes.  And they do. (Water trolls?)

{B} Stuff left behind by some monsters, once dead:
{B}  - Elf corpses should leave elvish stuff.

This is now fixed for later release (I think).

{B}  - Crocodiles should (sometimes) leave: a bag of holding, or leather
       armor or leather boots.

Seen any good wands of polymorph lately?

{B} Thanks.  Bruno  br0w+@andrew.cmu

Sure.						Norm.
